{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass. Here's the fix:\n\n**Root cause:** In `repo/query.py`, `build_query` used `if v:` to decide whether to emit a parameter. Since empty strings are falsy in Python, any key with an empty-string value (e.g. `?q=`) was silently dropped from the URL.\n\n**Fix:** Changed the guard to `if v is None: continue` so that only `None` values are dropped, while empty strings are emitted as `key=`.\n\n```python\ndef build_query(params):\n    \"\"\"Return a sorted ``key=value`` query string for a params dict.\n\n    A value of ``None`` is dropped; an empty string is emitted as ``key=``\n    so that empty query parameters are preserved on the request URL.\n    \"\"\"\n    parts = []\n    for k in sorted(params):\n        v = params[k]\n        if v is None:\n            continue\n        parts.append(f\"{k}={v}\")\n    return \"&\".join(parts)\n```\n\nThis preserves `{\"q\": \"\", \"p\": \"1\"}` → `\"p=1&q=\"` while still dropping `None` values."}]},"session_id":"790a418b-b158-4282-bb52-ff381e2a8262"}
